div.p:
“The immense number of the Spanish steamers (over forty steamers now running);
                    their capacity, as most of them carry twice the cargo of an American steamer;
                    the circumstance of paying the tonnage dues in the United States only once a
                    year, they get full cargoes in Cuba to the United States and leaving from the
                    United States to their European port also with full cargoes,—allows them to
                    accept freight in Cuba at rates much more equitable than formerly paid.”
